extraction_notes: |
  - Printed 62-64 (cache p063-p065), read from the text layer. The survey flags
    cache p064 (printed 63) as corrupt; it was rendered at 200 dpi, and the flag
    is the artist''s signature under the illustration. Every number on that page
    - 6D6 per 12 hours, 1,200 feet, attacks at 3/6/9/12/15, the bonus line and
    the first eight skills - matches the text layer. The attribute block on
    printed 62 was also checked against a render.
  - The Haven Mutant rules on printed 60 apply to all eight mutant R.C.C.s: G.M.
    approval, no O.C.C., no power armor or robots, no Juicer or M.O.M.
    conversion. They are in `restrictions`.
  - `xp_table` is the Haven Mutant ladder on printed 79 (the one for every
    mutant but the Shaman), stored as the lower bound of each band.
  - Attacks are "Instinctive": five at level one, stored as
    `combat.attacks_base`, with +1 at levels 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15. No Hand to Hand
    skill is printed.
  - Bonuses are the dry-land figures. The book doubles them underwater; that is
    conditional and is a special ability. The +4 save against poison, pollution and
    drugs is stored as toxins_poisons 4 and harmful_drugs 4.
  - Psionics: two named powers granted outright with I.S.P. of M.E. x10 +1D6
    per level. No `type` is stated, because the book says the Dyno-Man is not
    considered psychic and saves against psionics at 15. The pool formula has
    no dice of its own, so the per-level 1D6 is also rolled once at creation
    (level one reads 1D6 above M.E. x10); the book''s line is ambiguous on
    whether level one gets it, and this reading was accepted rather than
    restated.
  - Spd underwater (2D4x10) and Horror Factor 14 for a party of at least six are
    prose; the stored Spd is the land figure.
  - Prowl''s +15% applies underwater only, so the stored Prowl is the catalog
    base and the bonus is in its note.
  - Secondary skills: the book rolls 1D4+3. `count` is a number, so the maximum
    (7) is stored and the roll is in the note. Decided at import; revisit if the
    picker is ever given a rolled count.
  - W.P. ancient versus modern is recorded in the choice-group notes, because
    the catalog does not split the Weapon Proficiencies category.
  - Money: none; `starting_money` is 0. The 1D4x1000 in tradable goods is prose
    in GM Notes.
  - Starting gear not stored as rows: the Mutant Bone Spear, Bone Knife and
    Bone Shiv (bone weapon rows arrive with the gear PR), one weapon per W.P.,
    1D6 days of food and water, an optional loincloth and cloak or cape, and
    personal items. They are listed in GM Notes.
  - Shaman variant: its skills are added by the variant; the removal of Secondary, Piloting and modern W.P. skills, the prayers and the Shaman XP ladder are prose only; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F108.
  - Shaman variant: the +3D6+10 P.P.E. is folded into the variant''s own
    `ppe_base` because the pool parser reads one dice term and the class''s own
    formula has none; the +1D6 per level is in the same formula. The +2 I.Q.
    and +1D4+2 M.A. are attribute bonuses on the variant, which restates the
    class''s other bonuses because a variant''s bonuses replace the class''s.
---

## Lore

Dyno-Men are some of the oddest of the Haven Mutants: huge, hairless,
finely scaled humanoids shaped like a theropod dinosaur, as comfortable in the
water as on land. A neck almost as long as the body carries a head that looks
more like a monstrous sea lion than a man - tiny eyes, a nose that is little
more than a sealing flap, a mouth of a hundred small teeth, and two tentacle
feelers drooping like a mustache. Webbed hands and feet and a heavy rudder of a
tail make them slow on land and swift below the surface. The skin is pale gray
with a pink belly, throat and face, marked in near-black green.

They blame technology for humanity''s fall and magic for the monsters that
followed, and so they reject both. They see ordinary humans as a spent people
and the mutants as the heirs who will replace them - which puts the Coalition
at the top of their list of offenders, the Magic Zone''s spell casters next, and
the Mystic Knights after that.

## GM Notes

On the surface they wear headdresses built from big animal skulls, bones, fins,
claws and teeth, and little else, and they seldom carry weapons or tools.

- **Alignment:** any; most are Unprincipled (10%), Anarchist (30%), Aberrant
  (20%) or Miscreant (30%), the rest other alignments. Quick to anger, intolerant
  of humans and D-Bees, and fiercely loyal to the Shamans, to mutantkind and to
  Madhaven.
- **Size:** 7-8 feet (2.1-2.4 m) at the shoulder, with a neck of the same length
  usually carried bent forward so the head sits 9-10 feet (2.7-3 m) up with a
  7-8 foot reach, and a 7-9 foot (2.1-2.7 m) tail dragging behind on land. 700
  to 1,200 lbs (315-540 kg).
- **Life span:** could reach 140, but the average is 2D6+56 for males and
  2D6+60 for females.
- **Average NPC level:** 1D4+2. Player characters start at level one.
- **Money:** none, but 1D4x1000 in tradable goods - pre-Rifts curios, loot from
  outsiders, or fish.
- **Other gear:** a Mutant Bone Spear, Bone Knife and Bone Shiv, one weapon for
  each W.P., 1D6 days of food and water, and at most a loincloth and a cloak or
  cape.
- **Habitat:** ruins, bridges, broken docks and the waterways. They spend about
  half their time in the water but can stay on land for weeks, and make homes
  under concrete slabs, in basements, sewers and tunnels.
- **Allies and enemies:** as the other Haven Mutants - amicable with fellow
  mutants, wary of the Knights of the White Rose (with the added sin, for a
  Dyno-Man, that the Knights use technology), and trading with the Horune
  Pirates and Splugorth slavers without trusting them. Their foes are
  outsiders, ghosts, monsters, Undead Horrors, madmen and creatures of magic.

## Mutant Shaman

Every sizable clan is led by a Shaman, who keeps the race''s own attributes and
powers and gains the following. Choose the **Dyno-Man Shaman** variant.

- **Attributes and P.P.E.:** +2 I.Q., +1D4+2 M.A., +3D6+10 starting P.P.E. and
  +1D6 P.P.E. per level. The variant carries these.
- **Shaman skills:** Animal Husbandry (+10%), Literacy in the native language
  (American, +15%), Brewing: Medicinal (+15%), Dance (+10%), Fasting (+20%),
  History: Pre-Rifts (+10%), Holistic Medicine (+10%), History:
  Post-Apocalypse (+20%), Sing (+10%), Public Speaking (+20%) and Veterinary Science (+10%). The
  variant adds these.
- **What they replace:** these skills take the place of ALL Secondary Skills,
  all Piloting skills and all modern W.P.s. A Shaman never uses a modern weapon,
  vehicle or machine. The app cannot remove skills through a variant, so a
  Shaman player should leave the secondary picks and the modern W.P. pick
  empty; the Dyno-Man''s paddle-boat skill is a Piloting skill and is lost too.
- **Role:** Shamans make the clan''s laws, judge its disputes and lead the clan
  and tribe.
- **Prayers to Isis, the Mighty Lady.** Prayer of Strength: 01-20%, +5% per
  level, to be heard; if it is, +6 P.S., +1D4x10 M.D.C., and 48 hours without
  food or water with no ill effect. Usable up to six times a year. Prayer of
  Inspiration or Wisdom: 01-12%, +3% per level (+10% after a week of fasting);
  if heard, a dream vision brings insight, an idea or a caution concerning
  whatever was prayed about.
- **Experience:** a Shaman advances on the "Gateway Knight & Mutant Shaman"
  ladder (printed 79), not the Haven Mutant one: 0, 2,351, 4,701, 9,401,
  18,801, 28,001, 38,001, 53,001, 77,001, 102,001, 143,001, 195,201, 240,401,
  310,601, 360,801.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dyno-men');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dyno-men';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-dyno-men-class.sql');
